      "body": "## What\n\n- Raises `max-parallel` from 1 so these shards run at the same time instead of one after another:\n  - `stage-b-test-1-gpu-large-amd`: 3\n  - `stage-b-test-2-gpu-large-amd`: 2\n  - `multimodal-gen-test-1-gpu-amd`: 2\n  - `multimodal-gen-test-2-gpu-amd`: 2\n- Trims `stage-a-test-1-gpu-small-amd` to the two server sanity tests, as CUDA's base-a does. The seven AMD kernel/unit tests move to `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd`.\n\n## Why\n\nOn PRs the ROCm matrix is only rocm10, so `max-parallel: 1` serializes the shards:\n- 1-gpu-large runs 3 × ~35 min back to back, which is most of why `wait-for-stage-b-amd` finishes around minute 117.\n- The 2-GPU diffusion job runs 2 × ~2 h back to back.\n\nThe cap came in with the ROCm-version matrix consolidation in #38632. Scheduled runs with two ROCm versions will now use up to 2–3 runners at once for these jobs instead of 1.\n\nEvery other stage waits on stage-a, so its runtime is on the critical path of every PR. The moved tests are small and unchanged.\n\nRelated: #46084, #46085. #46084 cuts 1-gpu-large to 2 shards and 2-gpu-large to 1; the new limits are harmless either way, and the branches merge cleanly.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] `pr-test-amd.yml` dispatch of `stage-a-test-1-gpu-small-amd`, `stage-b-test-1-gpu-large-amd`, `stage-b-test-2-gpu-large-amd` (rocm10): pending\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39978195338](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39978195338)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39978195542](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39978195542)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39978195373](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39978195373)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
